  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "flb_parser_create",
    "file": "fluent-bit/src/flb_parser.c",
    "description": "`flb_parser_create` inconsistently transfers ownership of the caller-supplied decoder list on failure. It stores `decoders` in `p->decoders` immediately (line 149), then a later validation failure\u2014here, rejection of `time_offset`\u2014calls `flb_parser_destroy(p)`, which destroys and frees that list. The function nevertheless returns NULL, and callers treat NULL as meaning creation did not take ownership and destroy the original list themselves. The second destruction enters `flb_parser_decoder_list_destroy` with a freed list and causes the reported heap-use-after-free. Ownership should only be committed on successful creation, or failure cleanup must leave caller-owned inputs untouched/clearly null them consistently.",
    "conditions": "The fuzz input selects construction of a non-NULL decoder list in `parser_fuzzer.c`, selects a non-NULL `time_offset`, and supplies an invalid offset whose first byte is neither `Z`, `+`, nor `-`. The harness passes the list and offset to `flb_parser_create`; the function assigns the list to the partially built parser, `flb_parser_tzone_offset` returns -1, and `flb_parser_create` calls `flb_parser_destroy`, freeing the decoder list before returning NULL. The harness's NULL-result cleanup then calls `flb_parser_decoder_list_destroy(list)` again, triggering the UAF. The production `parser_conf_file` failure path has the same caller-cleanup ownership expectation."
  },
